# 20 — Tests: authoring, proving, running

The binding text of J1–J9 is `docs/features/e2e-harness.md` §Authoring laws — read it before touching
anything under `e2e/**` (specs OR helpers). This rule restates the laws and adds the ones a unit test
must obey too.

## The nine laws (J1–J9)

- J1 Every mutable fixture is namespaced run × job (`E2E_SHARD`) × worker × project × test tag;
  every scratch slug/key starts with `e2e-` (a letters-only prefix where a door forbids digits).
- J2 Global-sweep tests run in a fence language per project; real catalogue keys are read-only.
- J3 Never edit a real reference row in ANY project (a seeded plan, category, location, language,
  user); per-axes scratch entities, deleted in a hook that survives a timeout (`afterEach`, not only
  a body `finally`) by a destroy that throws on failure; the shard-1 setup alone reaps residue.
- J4 Bulk/count assertions read per-key DB truth via the service client; summaries are asserted for
  visibility only; mismatches throw with the page/query-cache/audit dump.
- J5 Locators via the viewport-aware twin helpers, never a bare prefix + `.first()`; fixtures via
  service-client TABLE operations; bulk tests carry a budget and named phases; anchor on structure,
  never English text.
- J6 Tests mutating a global list run in ONE project; invariants and public-surface anchors exclude
  other tests' rows; never locate a real row by its position on a shared roster (search or DB truth).
- J7 Seed before navigate; assert seeded rows render before acting; polls shorter than the budget
  so failures assert with values; Playwright's built-in waiting only — never `waitForTimeout`.
- J8 `@global-state` tests run serial-only in the nightly; flaky passes are ledgered, and three in
  seven days is an incident.
- J9 Identity: the pool (`leaseUser()`) for consumers — at most TWO pooled accounts per test; tests
  that mutate their own auth state carry `@private-identity` and take the real door.

## Proof laws

- Real rows are never fixtures — in tests AND in migration proofs.
- No weakened proof: an assertion is never loosened to pass; a timeout is never raised without a
  named cause; a rate dial is never raised for a test (it gets a `rate_overrides` row for its own
  user); an allowlist or census entry always names the test that provokes it.
- A refusal test proves the refused side effect did NOT happen: no parse, no dial spent, no RPC, no
  provider call, no row written, no storage object, no audit row.
- Red-first: a test that reproduces a defect is shown failing against the previous code (a local run
  against the old commit or constant; nothing reverted is ever committed), then green. A test for new
  behaviour needs no red run. A test that cannot be shown red carries a positive control.
- A test's premise is measured AFTER its own fixture is in place: a fixture that changes the layout
  or roster it measures (a scratch root joining the menu, a seeded row joining a list) is seeded
  first, then the page is read (INC-1015).
- Tests see what a person sees: typed by keyboard, boxes measured, nothing read while an animation
  runs (`settled(page)` after an overlay opens, and after any press or click before a computed style
  is read: the press fades out over 120 ms, and SGB-5 read a colour mid-fade in turn C1); every box a test compares is read together in one
  frame through `layoutBoxes({ name: locator, … })` (`e2e/helpers/ui.ts`), never `boundingBox()` one
  by one.
- Fixtures are captured from real tool output, never authored. A fixture or text that moves between
  files is copied by script with a sha256 before and after.
- Tests set their own environment: every test that reaches a provider path sets the key or stand-in
  flag it needs with `vi.stubEnv` and restores it; none relies on the process environment.
- Spec files are edited by hand, never by search-and-replace; a spec change the brief did not
  enumerate is a STOP naming the test and line. `test.only` never lands.
- New test ids: before you assign one, grep the `it(` / `test(` titles in `src/`, `e2e/` and
  `scripts/`; a collision is renamed (TI-1, `scripts/test-ids.test.ts`, fails on any id used twice:
  B2 and C1 both lost a CI run to it). No spec file carries more than ~25 tests — split by area,
  titles and bodies intact, hooks travelling with their tests.
- Behaviour-preserving moves keep assertions byte for byte; a test whose mock must change shape is
  listed in the report with its id and reason.
- Evidence survives a timeout: a full-walk test attaches its per-step ladder from `afterEach` via
  `test.info().attach`; every click inside a retry loop is a bounded attempt.

## Harness helpers you must use (never re-implement)

`gotoReady` / `findRow` (the render invariant: no `[object Object]`, `undefined`, `NaN`);
`layoutBoxes` and `settled` (`e2e/helpers/ui.ts`); `awaitDraftSaved(page)` before polling DB truth or
navigating after a wizard change; `stopPageBeforePurge(page)` before a hook purges drafts;
`inOneWindow(windowSeconds, needMs, tag)` before counted dial calls; `withinPreviewBudget` for import
previews (only IG-3 drives the limit, never raised); `staleStepUpOnClient` / `afterTotpStep`;
`awaitConsole(page)` for the countries console; `finderStub`; `releaseStaleScratchAlias` for
fixed-slot fixtures; `chunkByLength(values, 4000)` on every unbounded `.in(...)`; `retryingFetch` on
every service-role client; the category menu's one reader (`e2e/helpers/category-menu.ts`);
`stripScratchRows` for whole-export comparisons; `anchorRealRow` / category search instead of page
position; `pickCity` (`e2e/helpers/posting.ts`) for the place step; `switchLanguage`
(`e2e/helpers/ui.ts`); a route handler that fetches the real answer goes through `whilePageLives`
(`e2e/helpers/route-guard.ts`). A table with a person column has its RESET or EXEMPT line in
`e2e/helpers/pool-reset-map.ts`.

## Running tests

- Unit: `bun run test:unit` (vitest, the whole suite) at THE CHECKS; while iterating, a touched
  file's tests alone (`bunx vitest run <file>`), and the laws (`bunx vitest run scripts
  --maxWorkers=2`: the test ids, the censuses, the allowlists) after any change to a test, a guard,
  an allowlist or a shared mechanism.
- Browser tests start ONLY with `bun run e2e:local -- <spec files>` or `bun run e2e:changed` (when
  `scripts/e2e-select.ts` prints five files or fewer) — never plain `playwright test` or
  `bun run test:e2e` (the committed `.env` points at production and the setup refuses it). Target:
  ethio-staging, through `E2E_SUPABASE_URL`, `E2E_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` and
  `E2E_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in the environment (on this computer the operator may keep them in
  `~/.ethio-e2e.env`, loaded by the shell; you check only that the three names are set, never their
  values) — never `supabase/config.toml`, never production. Both projects (`mobile-360`, `desktop-1280`), 2 workers, fake mode, 0 retries; each
  touched spec file whole and alone; named ids by `--grep`. Paste every count line and the server
  log's `[ssr-error]` count by path.
- A spec file not fully green is not committed.
- Repeats: a changed spec's repeatability is proven by CI's repeat lane (DEC-283), never by local
  `--repeat-each` runs; the operator-dispatched Flake check is for investigations only.
- "STAGING BEHIND: apply <file>" from the preflight is the supervisor's staging step, never a code
  fix: STOP and report the apply line.
- `bun run e2e:local` also needs a Chromium (`bunx playwright install chromium` once per
  environment, or `E2E_CHROMIUM_PATH`), port 4173 free and fresh i18n maps. When any is missing, say
  so; never improvise a target.
- A partial or killed run is reported as partial and never re-run in the background; CI on the
  pull request and on dev runs every test in its lanes.
